 "note": "MSQ lists Heron Island as a secondary place of Gladstone (80 km west-south-west, in the Port Curtis harbour) with high and low water 33 minutes earlier and 0.71 of its range. Bundaberg's standard port gauge at Burnett Heads (24 46 S 152 23 E, 153 km south-south-east) is used instead because its tide is closer to Heron's in both respects: MSQ's 2026 tidal planes put spring high and low water at +1.21 and -1.09 m about mean sea level at Heron Island, +1.16 and -1.17 m at Burnett Heads and +1.62 and -1.62 m at Gladstone, and in the 2026 fits Burnett Heads' M2 runs about 43 minutes ahead of Gladstone's, so about 10 minutes ahead of Heron's where Gladstone's lags by 33. Neither is an offshore gauge; times and heights at Heron Island differ from Burnett Heads' by those amounts. (The portal's 2024 and 2025 resources of the separate 'Burnett Heads' storm-surge gauge hold Bugatti Reef Outer's file, so they are not used.)",
